  "title": "Cesar Chavez",
  "summary": "Cesar Chavez was born near Yuma, Arizona, in 1927 and grew up as a migrant farm worker. In 1962 he founded the National Farm Workers Association, later the United Farm Workers. It joined the 1965 Delano grape strike. He died near Yuma in April 1993 and was buried at La Paz.",
